  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY NIGHT THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 244 AM CDT Thu Sep 3 2026\n\nModel guidance remains in good agreement with a weak cold front \nmoving through the area Saturday night. The NBM 25th/75th percentile \ntemperature forecast at St. Louis for both Saturday and Sunday is \nstill only showing 3-5 degree spread. Most areas will remain dry as \nonly 15-20% of the LREF members are producing rain on Saturday night \nand Sunday.  Temperatures will still be unseasonably hot Sunday and \nMonday with highs in the lower to middle 90s.  Dewpoints will be \nslower to drop with the easterly winds and readings mainly in the \n70s on Sunday versus 60s on Monday.  This will result in heat \nindexes on Sunday over parts of the area still climbing over 100 \ndegrees which may require an extension to the going headlines. \nTemperatures will climb back into the middle 90s by the middle \nof next week as the upper high builds back into the area. Highs \nwill be close to records again over parts of the area. The upper\nhigh will also keep the area dry through the middle of next \nweek.",
